{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "Footnote 4 is supplied at db43e253bea18.u30.8235; the advertising claim's uncertainty statement incorrectly calls it missing. It incorporates FAQs and other SFC guidance, whose texts are missing.",
    "The gift-control authorities themselves are not supplied: paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct and the answer to question 1 of the SFC's 30 September 2010 FAQs, identified in footnote 3. The circular supports its stated rule, but does not establish the complete external interpretive standard.",
    "Scope placement changes executable answers. node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e returns OUT_OF_SCOPE for an unoffered component; node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f does so for an unlinked component; node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5 and node.bca408c75cbf8467afafada6 do so for an unlinked offer. Their typed questions instead admit a negative answer for no caught component. Clarify whether these are intentional assessment prerequisites or conditions that should produce FALSE.",
    "node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5 similarly returns OUT_OF_SCOPE when the promotional link is false. Its compliance result must remain confined to the selected gift control and must not imply compliance with section 103 or advertising requirements.",
    "The offer-level candidates combine an offer-level promotional link with an existential non-discount gift classification. For mixed offers, these facts must establish that the same gift component has the required promotional connection; otherwise they can catch an unrelated component.",
    "The SFC-authorised-fund limitations have support in the circular's introductory definition and selected context. They should not be presented as establishing the full scope of paragraph 3.11 for all investment products.",
    "The packet does not establish an effective source interval. The candidates' temporal-basis statements therefore remain unverified."
  ],
